course: dictionary
lesson: 5788
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «ma» can mean a mother, a university degree, or a unit used in science. To find the right meaning, look at the context: the words and sentences around it.
explain: In an old American story, «Ma» and «Pa» are what children call their parents. Here «Ma» means mother, like «Mum». Mum is the informal word for mother in English, and «ma» is heard in old stories, in the USA countryside and in Ireland.
explain: The spelling and the place it is used also give clues. «MA» with capital letters is a Master of Arts, a university degree. «mA» with a small m is a milliamp, a tiny unit of electric current, used in science. Other languages also use «ma»: in French «ma mère» means «my mother», and in Italian «ma» means «but».
fact: One word can have several meanings, so context tells you which one you need.
fact: Informal «ma» means mother, like «Mum».
fact: «MA» stands for Master of Arts, a university degree.
fact: «mA» is a milliamp, a tiny unit of electric current in science.
fact: In French, «ma» means «my» before a feminine noun, as in «ma mère».
exercise: In an old American story, children call their parents «Ma» and «Pa». What does ma mean here? | My | A university degree | *Mother | A tiny unit of electric current
exercise: In a science lesson you read «The bulb uses 20 mA of current.» What does mA mean? | My | Master of Arts | *A milliamp, a tiny unit of electric current | Mother
exercise: In Mandarin you read «nǐ hǎo ma?» What does the little ma at the end do? | It makes the sentence louder | It means mother | *It turns the sentence into a question | It means but
test: In Italian, «ma» appears in the sentence «Ma, I want to come too.» What does it mean? | My | Degree | *But | Mother
test: On a graduate's card you read «MA». What does it stand for? | Milliamp | Mother | *Master of Arts | My
exam: Why does «ma» mean «my» in «ma mère», but «MA» means Master of Arts on a card? | They are the same word, so either meaning always works | Only the capital letters matter | *The words and spelling around the word show which meaning you need | Ma always means mother
